---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";

const CONTACT_REQUEST = "https://github.com/ayaangazali/eyes/issues/115";
---

<Layout title="Eyes privacy policy" description="What Eyes keeps about workers and agents, for how long, and who sees it.">
  <main class="legal">
    <h1 class="m-0 text-4xl font-semibold tracking-[-0.03em] md:text-5xl">Privacy policy</h1>
    <p class="mt-3">Last updated: October 23, 2026</p>

    <h2>Who this covers</h2>
    <p>
      Eyes is a hackathon project. It connects AI agents with people nearby ("workers") who send a live photo of a public
      place. This policy covers workers, agents and the people who own agent API keys. Payments run in Stripe test mode
      today, so no real money moves yet.
    </p>

    <h2>What we keep about workers</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>When you join: your name, mobile number and the location you shared. Your email is optional.</li>
      <li>If you add an email: the address, and the time you confirmed it. An email you never confirm is dropped after 24 hours.</li>
      <li>
        Your latest spot: each task photo, each tap on an Eyes "Update my spot" link, each Apple or Google Maps link
        or "lat, lng" pair you text us, and the Eyes location automations or app (if you set them up) replace it. We keep
        only the latest spot, never a history.
      </li>
      <li>When you do a task: your photo, your answer, your GPS position and the time you took the photo.</li>
      <li>
        If you text HELP about a held answer: that text and any replies you add, kept with the review ticket for Eyes
        staff.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>How long we keep worker data</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Our photo moderation blocks only confirmed graphic gore or explicit sexual content. Faces alone are not blocked.</li>
      <li>
        Submitted photos, answers and task records have no automatic expiry, including photos held for review. A photo
        that has not passed moderation is not sent to the agent; Eyes staff can review it. Links to photos shared with
        the agent have no automatic expiry.
      </li>
      <li>
        Texting STOP stops task texts, deletes your latest spot and your email, and turns off your location codes. It does not
        delete your name, number or past tasks.
      </li>
      <li>Your email stays until you reply STOP (by text or email) or we remove you. An email you never confirm is dropped after 24 hours.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>How we use worker data</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        Your latest spot picks which tasks we text you; a spot older than 24 hours is not used. Eyes staff see it as an
        unlabeled dot on our live map.
      </li>
      <li>
        The AI agent that asked gets your answer, the time and how far you were from the place. It gets your photo only
        if the photo passes moderation. It never gets your name or number.
      </li>
      <li>We use your email for task offers, capture links, paid notices and the sign-in link to /me. The AI agent never gets your email.</li>
      <li>Stripe collects your payout details directly. Eyes does not store your bank details.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Your iPhone's device ID (only if you install the Eyes app)</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        A device ID (UDID) is a number Apple gives each iPhone.
        Registering your iPhone sends it to Eyes, with the iPhone model and iOS version.
      </li>
      <li>
        We keep it only to let that iPhone install the Eyes app outside the App Store.
        Apple requires each such iPhone to be registered by its device ID.
      </li>
      <li>It goes to two places: the device list in Eyes' Apple developer account, and the Eyes database.</li>
      <li>
        Texting STOP deletes it from the Eyes database.
        Apple's device list keeps it until our Apple membership year renews, because Apple only lets us remove devices then.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>What we keep about agents</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>The agent's name and its owner's email address.</li>
      <li>A hash of the API key, never the key itself.</li>
      <li>The balance and a ledger of every top up, escrow, refund, payout and fee.</li>
      <li>The tasks the agent created and the questions it asked.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Service providers</h2>
    <p>These companies process data so Eyes can run:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>InsForge: the database and photo storage.</li>
      <li>Inkbox: iMessage texts to workers, and email when Primitive can't send it.</li>
      <li>Primitive: email for agents and workers.</li>
      <li>Stripe: payments and worker payouts.</li>
      <li>Manufact Cloud: hosting for the MCP/API server.</li>
      <li>Cloudflare: edge routing, hosting for eyes.pictures and app.eyes.pictures, and Workers AI for the safety and photo checks.</li>
      <li>Anthropic: a second opinion AI check on tasks and photos, when it is turned on.</li>
      <li>OpenStreetMap Nominatim: turning place names into coordinates.</li>
      <li>Apple: registering iPhone device IDs for installation outside the App Store.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>This website</h2>
    <p>
      Eyes uses Cloudflare Web Analytics to measure website visits and page performance.
      Cloudflare adds its analytics script automatically, including on eyes.pictures and app.eyes.pictures.
      It reports page views, load times, referring sites, country, browser, operating system and device type.
      See <a class="ui-link" href="https://developers.cloudflare.com/web-analytics/data-metrics/">Cloudflare's data and metrics documentation</a>.
      Fonts and images are served from the same site.
    </p>

    <h2>Your choices</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Reply STOP to any Eyes text or email to stop task texts and delete your email. Reply START to a text to turn them back on.</li>
      <li>Your mobile number is tied to your account. You can't change it yourself; text HELP to ask.</li>
      <li>Your email is optional, one per account.</li>
      <li>Photograph public places. Avoid photographing private individuals without their permission; faces alone do not cause automatic rejection or deletion.</li>
      <li>For data and deletion requests, see the contact notice below. Do not post personal data in public issues.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Changes</h2>
    <p>We will update this policy and the date above when what we keep changes, and before real payments start.</p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
      We have not yet published a private address for data and deletion requests.
      This requirement remains open in <a class="ui-link" href={CONTACT_REQUEST}>issue #115</a>.
      That issue is public, not a private request channel. Do not post personal data there.
      Workers can reply HELP to an Eyes text or email for help with using Eyes.
    </p>
  </main>
</Layout>
